B08d11 — isolated configuration API supplement, 2026-09-28
=========================================================

The original API build fails because unistd.h lacks _SC_XOPEN_UUCP and
_PC_TIMESTAMP_RESOLUTION. This separately approved dependency configuration
adds unused names 251 and 21 in the pinned musl namespace and implements their
runtime dispatch; it does not edit the original headers, archives or receipt.
These numeric values are not promised to match another libc's private ABI.

_SC_XOPEN_UUCP returns -1 without changing errno: the configuration does not
provide UUCP. _PC_TIMESTAMP_RESOLUTION supports Linux tmpfs (1 ns), follows
path symlinks via O_PATH, checks real descriptors, and preserves success errno.
Other filesystem associations return -1/EINVAL, never a guessed 1 ns/1 s or an
incorrect "unlimited" result. There is no claim of all-filesystem support.
Linux statfs does not expose s_time_gran. The frozen Linux source establishes
shmem's value explicitly at mm/shmem.c:5123 (s_time_gran=1), hash below.

The POSIX interface requires both names. Its timestamp query is not a generic
indefinite maximum/minimum: returning -1 unchanged-errno merely to make a new
header compile would misstate this contract. The bounded association refusal
uses the documented EINVAL boundary. Sources:
  https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/fpathconf.3p.html
    Authorized reproduction of IEEE/The Open Group POSIX.1-2017 text.
  https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/sysconf.html
  https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9799919799/basedefs/unistd.h.html
No POSIX.1-2024 feature level is advertised by this patch.

RED runtime control uses the new names with the untouched original archives:
13/27 focused assertions fail in each of 12 executions. Existing original
unistd.o.err separately records both missing-name compiler errors. The initial
red directory also retains a malformed patch-file rejection; that is not a
runtime/compiler RED. The subsequent -red-...b directory is the runtime RED.

GREEN: GCC14/Clang19/EvoCC, O0/O2, reference/mixed archive bases:
  324/324 focused checks PASS (12 executions, 27 checks each).
  12/12 original api/main linked executions PASS.
  All 79 original API translation-unit objects participate: 78 unchanged
  reference objects plus the recompiled, unchanged api/unistd.c. This is NOT
  a claim that EvoCC compiled all 79 API objects. Its unistd.c is typechecked
  with EvoCC's existing C99 driver contract, not GCC diagnostic emulation.
  The probe checks errno, nanosecond timestamps, symlink following, unlinked
  open files, closed FDs, missing/empty paths, unknown names, unsupported
  procfs associations and old-name regression controls.

GCC retains the original -pedantic-errors/-Werror/-Wno-unused API check.
Clang19 additionally diagnoses the legal C99 static void f() test wrapper;
the secondary Clang source-compatibility control explicitly adds
-Wno-strict-prototypes. Its initial rejection is retained in -green-... and
the flag is recorded in every final Clang argv; it is not silently called
identical diagnostic policy. No test source/assertion changed.

The common supplement verdict also requires each original API compilation,
the 79-object population and hashes, replacement-object link maps, all paired
executions and unchanged original inputs. Negative tests remove an object,
replace unistd.o, or fail compilation; none can PASS. All 303 ladder tests,
Ruff and git diff --check pass. No compiler source/spec was changed.

Recipe:
  python3 tools/ladder/musl_patched.py --suite conf \
    --evocc target/frontend/debug/evocc --output .build/floating-targeted/CONF-NEW
Use --unpatched-control for the old-library runtime control.
Raw final: .build/floating-targeted/musl-patched-conf-final-20260928/
Compiler/image identities are those in musl-patched-numerics.out.
